# Scope of this file: the PLAN (SubscriptionPlan) and the SCHOOL'S SUBSCRIPTION (SchoolSubscription) together
# with the quota that comes with them. Invoices / orders / payments are NOT here -- they are separate
# aggregates (Order, PaymentRecord, Invoice, SchoolBalance) and have their own schemas.
#
# Currency: every VND field is Float because the project has not declared any dedicated scalar for it. VND has no
# fractional unit so values are always whole, and numeric(15,0) at most still stays below 2^53, so a JS
# client reads them without losing precision. Moving to a BigDecimal scalar is a job for all 24 schemas
# together, not something to do piecemeal here.

enum SubscriptionPlanStatus {
    DRAFT
    ACTIVE
    ARCHIVED
}

enum SubscriptionPlanPeriod {
    DAY
    MONTH
    YEAR
}

enum SchoolSubscriptionStatus {
    ACTIVE
    EXPIRED
    CANCELLED
    "The System Admin forces loss of access IMMEDIATELY -- unlike CANCELLED, which only turns off renewal and still allows use until endDate"
    SUSPENDED
}

"""
Two school-level quota WALLETS, both in VND. Each activity is deducted from EXACTLY ONE wallet, and spending one
wallet does not touch the other -- so an unusually heavy week of speaking practice does not eat the assessment budget.

CLASS_TEST was removed: it is a SPENDING CEILING inside the ASSESSMENT wallet, not a third wallet, and it was charged the same amount
twice as ASSESSMENT for every class test. The ceiling per teacher still exists, in
SchoolSubscriptionQuotaUserAllocation with quotaType = ASSESSMENT.
"""
enum QuotaType {
    "Grading assessments -- both centralized assessments and in-class tests are deducted from here"
    ASSESSMENT
    "Students practicing speaking on their own"
    PRACTICE
}

type SubscriptionPlanQuota {
    id: ID!
    subscriptionPlanId: ID!
    quotaType: QuotaType!
    """
    The allowance included in the plan price, converted to VND. There is no longer a tokenUnitPrice next to it: the
    "VND per $1" unit price used to be an exchange rate with a margin added, which made the display differ from the
    real rate. Usage beyond the allowance is deducted straight from the school's balance at the rate recorded
    on each usage.
    """
    includedAmountVnd: Float!
}

type SubscriptionPlan {
    id: ID!
    name: String!
    tagline: String
    priceVnd: Float!
    """
    Plan cycle = periodType x periodCount (e.g. MONTH x 12). Replaces the old validityDays: a plan counted
    in months/years must expire on the matching calendar day, and adding a raw number of days drifts further over time.
    """
    periodType: SubscriptionPlanPeriod!
    periodCount: Int!
    maxTimePerAttemptMin: Int!
    status: SubscriptionPlanStatus!
    version: Int!
    createdAt: DateTime
    updatedAt: DateTime
    createdBy: ID
    updatedBy: ID
    "The replacement plan once this plan is ARCHIVED -- follow this chain to find a plan that can still be sold"
    replacedByPlanId: ID
    quotas: [SubscriptionPlanQuota!]!
}

type SubscriptionPlanPage {
    content: [SubscriptionPlanListItem!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

"""
One row in the plan list: the plan itself, together with the "most popular" label.

That label lives HERE and not on SubscriptionPlan because it is not a property of the plan -- it is the
result of comparing this plan with every other plan, and only has meaning in the context of a list. Ask for a
single plan (subscriptionPlan) and the question "is it the most popular" has no context to be answered in.
"""
type SubscriptionPlanListItem {
    subscription: SubscriptionPlan!
    """
    The plan used by the most schools ACROSS THE WHOLE SYSTEM (not the most in the current page), and not
    counted by the number of payments: a replaced plan gets a new id, so the transaction history stays on the
    old ARCHIVED plan. false for every plan while no school has subscribed.
    """
    isMostPopular: Boolean!
}

type SchoolSubscription {
    id: ID!
    schoolId: ID!
    subscriptionPlanId: ID!
    startDate: DateTime
    endDate: DateTime
    status: SchoolSubscriptionStatus!
    "The price paid at the time of purchase -- fixed, does not change with the plan price later"
    pricePaidSnapshot: Float!
    cancelledAt: DateTime
    createdAt: DateTime
    # The 3 suspended_* columns are wiped when the suspension is lifted, so they only reflect the suspension
    # that is CURRENTLY in effect, not the history. The durable history lives in school_subscription_events
    # (V2 section 12), written by ForceSuspend/UnsuspendSubscriptionUseCase -- not FinancialEvent, which was dropped.
    suspendedAt: DateTime
    suspendedReason: String
    suspendedBy: ID
    plan: SubscriptionPlan
    school: School
}

type SchoolSubscriptionPage {
    content: [SchoolSubscription!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

type SchoolSubscriptionQuotaRecord {
    id: ID!
    schoolSubscriptionId: ID!
    quotaType: QuotaType!
    "The allowance granted for this period, converted to VND"
    totalAllocatedAmountVnd: Float!
    """
    How many VND of the allowance above have been used. NEVER exceeds totalAllocatedAmountVnd: the part spent
    beyond the quota is moved by ConsumeQuotaService to the school's self-top-up wallet as an
    OVERAGE_CHARGE entry, rather than pushing this number above the ceiling.
    """
    usedAmountVnd: Float!
    """
    The part of totalAllocatedAmountVnd that the SCHOOL moved over from the wallet itself, instead of being granted by the plan (V12).

    After the first top-up, totalAllocatedAmountVnd mixes two sources, so this is the only number that
    answers "how much did the plan give, how much did the school add". It is also the ONLY part that survives
    the next renewal: the plan allowance is re-issued according to the new plan, while this part is carried
    over by the amount NOT YET SPENT (convention: plan money is spent first, self-topped-up money second).
    """
    fundedFromBalanceVnd: Float!
    # There is NO isLocked here anymore. It used to be the comparison usedAmountVnd > totalAllocatedAmountVnd,
    # a condition that can no longer happen (see above). "Is the school locked" is a SCHOOL-level fact --
    # the self-top-up wallet balance is negative, see SchoolSubscriptionDebtGuardService -- not a property of each
    # quota wallet, so this type has no right place for it.
}

"""
What the school gets if it renews right now -- seen BEFORE placing the order.

There is NO offset for leftover days: the new period CONTINUES the running one instead of overlapping it, so a
school that renews early loses no days and has nothing to be compensated for. startsAt states clearly when the
new period starts.
"""
type SchoolSubscriptionRenewalPreview {
    "true = the renewal plan differs from the current plan, i.e. the school is being moved to a replacement plan. The frontend should highlight this."
    planChanged: Boolean!
    "The plan the school is on / has just been on"
    currentPlan: SubscriptionPlan!
    "The plan that will be bought on renewal -- its id is exactly the acceptedPlanId that must be sent when placing the order"
    renewalPlan: SubscriptionPlan!
    "When the new period starts running: right now if no period is in effect, or the end date of the current period"
    startsAt: DateTime!
    "The price of the renewal plan, NOT including the service fee -- the fee is added when the order is placed"
    amountDue: Float!
}

"""
The PERSONAL quota of a user within a school-level wallet -- the spending ceiling the school places on the part of the wallet
this person may spend, NOT a separate wallet: the money still sits in the school-level wallet.

quotaType = ASSESSMENT only exists for teachers (the ceiling for the class tests they author), PRACTICE only exists for
students. Replaces the old pair MyClassTestQuotaAllocation/MyPracticeQuotaAllocation -- the same concept
needs only one type.
"""
type SchoolSubscriptionQuotaUserAllocation {
    id: ID!
    userId: ID!
    schoolSubscriptionId: ID!
    quotaType: QuotaType!
    allocatedAmountVnd: Float!
    usedAmountVnd: Float!
}

type QuotaPricing {
    estimatedCostPerAssessmentSecondUsd: Float!
    estimatedCostPerPracticeSecondUsd: Float!
    usdToVndRate: Float!
}

input SubscriptionPlanQuotaInput {
    quotaType: QuotaType!
    includedAmountVnd: Float!
}

input UpdateSubscriptionPlanInput {
    name: String
    tagline: String
    priceVnd: Float
    "periodType CANNOT be edited after creation (the period_type column is updatable = false) -- to change it, create a new plan and point replacedByPlanId at it"
    periodCount: Int
    maxTimePerAttemptMin: Int
    quotas: [SubscriptionPlanQuotaInput!]
}

extend type Query {
    subscriptionPlans(page: Int = 1, size: Int = 20): SubscriptionPlanPage!
    subscriptionPlan(id: ID!): SubscriptionPlan
    quotaPricing: QuotaPricing!

    schoolSubscriptions(
        keyword: String,
        subscriptionPlanId: ID,
        status: SchoolSubscriptionStatus,
        page: Int = 1,
        size: Int = 20
    ): SchoolSubscriptionPage!
    schoolSubscription(schoolId: ID!): SchoolSubscription
    schoolSubscriptionHistory(schoolId: ID!): [SchoolSubscription!]!

    subscriptionUsage(schoolId: ID!): [SchoolSubscriptionQuotaRecord!]!
    "null = the teacher has no separate personal quota, i.e. only the school's ASSESSMENT wallet applies"
    myAssessmentQuotaAllocation: SchoolSubscriptionQuotaUserAllocation
    "null = the school has NOT given this student a separate PRACTICE quota, i.e. the student is blocked completely"
    myPracticeQuotaAllocation: SchoolSubscriptionQuotaUserAllocation

    """
    What the school gets if it renews right now. Takes NO parameter: the plan to renew is the most recent
    plan of the school of the logged-in user.

    This query must be called BEFORE placing a renewal order: renewalPlan.id is exactly the acceptedPlanId that must be
    sent to POST /api/v1/orders/renewal. The plan in use may already be archived and assigned a replacement plan,
    in which case renewal switches to the new plan automatically -- the school must see it and agree first.
    """
    schoolSubscriptionRenewalPreview: SchoolSubscriptionRenewalPreview!
}

extend type Mutation {
    "Returns the id of the plan that was edited, not the whole object: the client queries again if needed -- see UpdateSubscriptionPlanUseCase."
    updateSubscriptionPlan(id: ID!, input: UpdateSubscriptionPlanInput!): ID!
}

"""
One person on the school's personal quota distribution screen.

A personal quota is a SPENDING CEILING that the school divides up internally, not a separate pocket of money: it holds
no money and produces no ledger entry. A person WITHOUT an allocation row is not blocked at the personal level, only the
school's quota wallet applies -- see ConsumeQuotaService.
"""
type SchoolQuotaUserAllocation {
    userId: ID!
    """
    null = NOT YET DISTRIBUTED (no row in the DB), completely different from 0 -- the two states give OPPOSITE
    behavior at the blocking gate.

    Not distributed means no personal blocking: a teacher spends freely from the school wallet
    (remainingUserAllocation returns null so the gate is skipped), while a student is the other way round --
    LEAST(...) in findPracticeSpendableFundsVnd pulls it down to 0 so not a single practice session is possible. A row
    that exists and equals 0 is blocked outright, for both types.

    The client must show two different labels. Collapsing them into the same 0 would hide the fact that half
    of the school's teachers currently have no spending ceiling at all.
    """
    allocatedAmountVnd: Float
    usedAmountVnd: Float!
    """
    The person the allocation belongs to. Joined through the userById data loader, so a page of N rows costs EXACTLY ONE
    extra users query, not N. null when the account has been removed from the system but the allocation row remains.
    """
    user: User
}

"""
One PAGE of the quota distribution screen, together with two totals for the whole set.

distributedAmountVnd must be computed by the server over the WHOLE set: the UI holds only one page, so adding up the
allocation column of that page gives a wrong number from the second page onward.
"""
type SchoolQuotaUserAllocationPage {
    "The school-level quota wallet -- ASSESSMENT when distributing to teachers, PRACTICE when distributing to students."
    pool: SchoolSubscriptionQuotaRecord!
    """
    The total distributed to people who are STILL eligible, over the whole set and not only this page.
    People who have left / graduated / changed role are NOT added -- see orphanedAmountVnd.
    """
    distributedAmountVnd: Float!
    """
    The part held under the names of people who are NO LONGER eligible. It does not count toward the ceiling and does not appear on
    any page of the table, so it must be said out loud: otherwise the total on the screen and the total of the rows differ
    with no one able to explain why. Usually 0.
    """
    orphanedAmountVnd: Float!
    """
    The school's distribution ceiling for this quota type, 0..1. Default 1.0 = the whole wallet can be distributed.
    It belongs to the SCHOOL, so it lives across every renewal -- see school_quota_policies (V5).
    """
    distributableRatio: Float!
    """
    The part of the wallet allowed to be distributed = pool x distributableRatio. Computed on the server because this is the number
    used to reject a distribution that exceeds the ceiling; letting the client multiply again opens the way for the two sides to disagree.
    """
    distributableAmountVnd: Float!
    """
    The amount of money the school can REALLY still pay for this quota type = the remaining plan quota + the self-top-up wallet
    balance (clamped at 0).

    COMPLETELY DIFFERENT from distributableAmountVnd: that ceiling is computed on total_allocated and does NOT shrink when the wallet is
    spent, so a school that has spent its wallet dry can still keep distributing up to the ceiling. Use it to WARN, not to
    block -- the personal spending ceiling must stay stable throughout the period, while the blocking already sits in the right place
    just before money is spent (ClassTestTokenQuotaGuardService / findPracticeSpendableFundsVnd).
    """
    spendableFundsVnd: Float!
    """
    The part of the school's SELF-TOPPED-UP wallet (school_balances) that CAN be eaten into beyond distributableAmountVnd when loosening the
    personal ceiling of ONE person -- not a reserved pocket of money, and SHARED by both ASSESSMENT and
    PRACTICE. Clamped to 0, negative is the school's debt (not an additional distributable part).
    """
    walletBalanceVnd: Float!
    content: [SchoolQuotaUserAllocation!]!
    page: Int!
    size: Int!
    totalElements: Int!
    totalPages: Int!
}

extend type Query {
    """
    The assessment quota distributed to each TEACHER, with paging.

    Replaces GET /v1/schools/{schoolId}/teachers/assessment-quota: that REST path returned every teacher
    in one go and did not carry the user's name, so the "Full name" column on the client was always empty.
    """
    schoolAssessmentQuotaUserAllocations(
        schoolId: ID!,
        "Filter by NAME. Leave empty to not filter."
        search: String,
        page: Int! = 1,
        size: Int! = 20
    ): SchoolQuotaUserAllocationPage!

    "The speaking-practice quota distributed to each STUDENT, with paging."
    schoolPracticeQuotaUserAllocations(
        schoolId: ID!,
        search: String,
        page: Int! = 1,
        size: Int! = 20
    ): SchoolQuotaUserAllocationPage!
}
